From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:27:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 307/311] avcodec: add a native AVS2 decoder for hardware
 acceleration

Add an AVS2 (GB/T 33475.2, IEEE 1857.4) decoder which parses the
sequence and picture headers in software and leaves the slice decoding
to a hardware accelerator, like the native AV1 decoder: there is no
software fallback, and it fails with ENOSYS when no hwaccel is
available. It is registered after libdavs2 so that a build with the
software decoder keeps preferring it.

The decoder removes the pseudo start code prevention bits of the
headers, parses the sequence header (reference configuration sets,
weighting quantization matrices) and the intra and inter picture
headers (RCS selection, picture structure, loop filter and chroma
quantizer offsets, the three weighting quantization data modes, the
adaptive loop filter parameters with the region to filter map), and
resolves the weighting quantization matrices that apply to each
picture. The default matrices and parameter sets are the normative
defaults of the standard.

It owns the decoded picture buffer: decode_order_index unwrapping, POC
derivation, reference lookup by DOI in RCS order, the background
picture (G, GB and S pictures), marking and removal including the
|delta POC| >= 128 rule, and output bumping in POC order driven by
picture_reorder_delay. Pictures whose references are missing before the
first intra picture (open GOP) are skipped, later ones are concealed
with the latest reference. A sequence header which changes the
picture format waits until the pictures of the old sequence have been
returned, then re-runs get_format().

Only progressive, frame coded 4:2:0 sequences are accepted. The
decoder exposes its context to the hwaccels: the picture header, the
resolved reference list with the per-picture reference POC lists the
hardware needs for temporal motion vector prediction, and the coded
picture (header and slices, with start codes) in the packet.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
